"answer": "Project Zenith is a groundbreaking initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole and initiated in Q3 2023. The project has received a $2M budget approval and a $15,000 training budget. The team was expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase, the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype, and a breakthrough in predictive analytics during Phase Two. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, have been updated to take effect in January. Various meetings were held for kickoff, budget allocation, onboarding, and milestone celebrations."
